// # X86-DOCS — Board alignment for the 2026-08-19 x86 repair pass
//
// Logline: SHIPPED.oot and ROADMAP.oot already name every x86 lock that the on-disk x86_emit_*.oo prove; the boards are honest today, so no board edit lands this pass.
//
// Setup: Read-only review of openOODA/SHIPPED.oot, openOODA/ROADMAP.oot, openOODA/audit/x86_phalanx.oot, oodac/x86_emit.oo, and the 13 x86_emit_*.oo siblings. C emit + gcc is the everyday path. Standalone x86_64 is the side emit, not a complete backend. Owner pinned overlay oodac/oodac 1755696 bytes (x86_phalanx.oot:25-27).
//
// Beats:
//   1. State what DOCS owns per x86_phalanx.oot:111-114.
//   2. Quote the x86 claims on SHIPPED.oot:34 by sub-line.
//   3. Quote the x86 claims on ROADMAP.oot by line.
//   4. Map each claim to on-disk x86_emit_*.oo + smoke by file:line.
//   5. Mark each claim [x]/[~]/[ ]/[?] with file:line evidence.
//   6. State honest mismatches, if any, by file:line.
//   7. List what is left to close the DOCS role.

// ============================================================
// 1. What DOCS owns (contract from x86_phalanx.oot §4)
// ============================================================

Per openOODA/audit/x86_phalanx.oot:111-114, the DOCS role owns:

  openOODA/SHIPPED.oot
  openOODA/ROADMAP.oot
  openOODA/audit/x86_docs.oot

  and explicitly: no guide/*.oot (the public-site lane).

DOCS keeps the boards honest about x86 state and writes this
audit file. COORD does not edit the boards (x86_phalanx.oot:115
names x86_coord.oot as the only COORD write; the same
disjoint rule as wasm_phalanx.oot:71 applies).

This file is read-only with respect to SHIPPED.oot and
ROADMAP.oot. The 2026-08-19 task spec also says
"Do not edit any existing file."

// ============================================================
// 2. SHIPPED.oot x86 claims (line by line)
// ============================================================

openOODA/SHIPPED.oot:34 is the single x86_64 product row.
It names, in this order:

  a) open69_hello.oo -> _start prints Hello; as+ld runs.
     Lock: scripts/open69_x86_smoke.oo.
  b) hello.oo -> fold greet+concat to
     "Hello, openOODA Developer!".
     Lock: scripts/x86_hello_smoke.oo.
  c) Harvest const ALU/if/let/mix including < <= >=
     as+ld. Locks: scripts/x86_*_smoke.oo.
  d) Leftover-ident, leftover-plus-print, while/for
     leftover ERR with no _start.
  e) Two-arg SysV snd: lea %rdi/%rsi then call.
     Lock: scripts/x86_snd_smoke.oo.
  f) Identity frame push %rbp / mov %rsp,%rbp / pop %rbp.
     Lock: scripts/x86_frame_smoke.oo.
  g) .bss bump concat yy+zz -> yyzz (.skip 4096, .Lcpy).
     Lock: scripts/x86_cat_smoke.oo.
  h) Overflow 2048+2048+1 ERR x86 buf no _start.
     Lock: scripts/x86_buf_ovf_smoke.oo.
  i) While/for leftover ERR (no silent once).
     Lock: scripts/x86_while_smoke.oo.
  j) println(greet("World")) is call greet and
     "Hello, World!". Lock: scripts/x86_greet_call_smoke.oo.
  k) hello.oo fold still has no call greet.
  l) Not emit-c. Not a complete x86 backend.
     AArch64 is residual. Lock: scripts/open69_x86_smoke.oo.

No other SHIPPED.oot line names x86.

