// ============================================================
// 4. On-disk x86_emit_*.oo state
// ============================================================

Entry (Cycle A+B partial C):
  oodac/x86_emit.oo:25-61 — pub fn x86_emit_stream. Order:
    x86_fold_hello -> x86_match_id_call (identity 1-arg)
    -> x86_match_snd_call (two-arg) -> x86_match_cat_call
    (.bss 4096) -> x86_match_greet_call -> x86_collect_prints.
    Empty src ERRs and exits 1 at :26-29. 61 lines.

Fold (DE2, new): oodac/x86_emit_fold.oo:177 — pub fn
  x86_fold_hello(src). RBRACE-tight greet shape; returns ""
  on any miss. 192 lines.

SysV (RT, new): oodac/x86_emit_sys.oo:14-67 — x86_ascii_esc
  (backslash, quote, newline, tab) and x86_emit_linux64
  (AT&T _start, SYS_write 1, SYS_exit 60). 68 lines.

Stack frame (Cycle C): oodac/x86_emit_frame.oo:13-21 —
  push %rbp / mov %rsp,%rbp and pop %rbp / ret. No `leave`
  and no libc. 21 lines.

Two-arg SysV snd (Cycle C): oodac/x86_emit_rsi.oo:19-249 —
  match two-arg String passthrough; lea %rdi / lea %rsi;
  call; mov %rsi,%rax; SYS_write from %rax. 248 lines.

.bss bump concat (Cycle C): oodac/x86_emit_str.oo:19-235 —
  match return a+b and println(cat(STRING, STRING)); copy
  both strings + newline into .Lbuf; 4096 cap; overflow ERRs.
  235 lines.

Greet call (Cycle C): oodac/x86_emit_greet.oo:19-242 — match
  return prefix+param+suffix; println of one STRING;
  lea .Lnm %rdi; call; copy into .Lbuf; 4096 cap; overflow
  ERRs. 242 lines.

Identity 1-arg (Cycle C): oodac/x86_emit_fn.oo:19-221 — match
  identity return of String param; lea %rdi, call, mov
  %rdi,%rax, SYS_write. 221 lines.

Const harvest (Cycle B+ partial C):
  oodac/x86_emit_walk.oo:13-214 — x86_collect_prints. Walks
  fn lets, mix, ALU, if, call, mut assign; leftover ERR even
  if msgs nonempty.
  oodac/x86_emit_harv.oo:17-214 — bind idx, negate, mix_try.
  oodac/x86_emit_alu.oo:17-248 — const ALU + - * / % paren.
  oodac/x86_emit_ctl.oo:18-215 — const if INT==INT and
  no-arg return scan.
  oodac/x86_emit_bind.oo:18-104 — same-fn let binds.
  oodac/x86_emit_span.oo:16-117 — ALU span and mix-paren.

All 14 emit files (1 entry + 13 helpers) are under 256 lines.
Largest: x86_emit_alu.oo and x86_emit_rsi.oo at 248.

Smoke set (ooda/scripts/): ~63 x86_*_smoke.oo files. Largest:
x86_int_div_smoke.oo and x86_int_rem_smoke.oo at 67 lines.

