// ============================================================
// 6. Honest mismatches
// ============================================================

None this pass. Every x86_emit_*.oo has a matching named
lock on the boards, and the five residual rows stay [ ].

The on-disk harvest does NOT const-fold calls. The fold
path is x86_emit_fold.oo:177 only, and the matchers in
x86_emit.oo:39-58 run AFTER the fold returns "". This
matches SHIPPED.oot:34 "hello.oo fold still has no
`call greet`." and x86_phalanx.oot:188 "Do not const-fold
calls (must emit lea and call)."

The on-disk harvest DOES refuse leftover (x86_emit_walk.oo:23
sets leftover_unresolved on any unfriendly token). This
matches SHIPPED.oot:34 and ROADMAP.oot:72.

The on-disk files do not exceed the 256-line cap. HYG owns
that audit. Two files sit at 248 lines (x86_emit_alu.oo,
x86_emit_rsi.oo).

